          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-73618",
          ":question/problem": "The row echelon form matrix $P$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 6 & -1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $P$ has $3$ pivots in the $2$nd, $4$th and $5$th columns:\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 6 & -1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot columns are the $1$st and $3$rd columns."
