              ":question/id": "ccfdc303-534f-530e-810b-f475a997f5d8",
              ":question/math-academy-id": "e-4703",
              ":question/problem": "The row echelon form matrix $B$ is given below. What are its pivot columns?\n\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n",
              ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $B$ has $3$ pivots in the $2$nd, $3$rd, and $4$th columns:\n\n\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{1} & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{-1} & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{1}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n"
            },
            ":knowledge-point/id": "488c9762-554b-5ea6-b414-ce6cbde9bbd1",
            ":knowledge-point/title": "Finding the Pivot Columns of a Matrix in Row Echelon Form"
          },
          {
            ":db/id": 17592186124478,
            ":knowledge-point/canonical-example": {
              ":db/id": 17592186124291,
              ":question/id": "22a77802-4114-516f-a0e0-4cda2e069361",
              ":question/math-academy-id": "e-4704",
              ":question/problem": "The row echelon form matrix $C$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n",
              ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $C$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th columns:\n\n\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{1} & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{5} & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $2$nd column."
            },
            ":knowledge-point/id": "a5f0d2e9-1cf6-5fe4-85cc-f401382f39b2",
            ":knowledge-point/title": "Finding the Non-Pivot Columns of a Matrix in Row Echelon Form"
          },
          {
            ":db/id": 17592186124479,
            ":knowledge-point/canonical-example": {
              ":db/id": 17592186124292,
              ":question/id": "6e4b2e85-86a8-5050-a60a-ae8d40453ad0",
              ":question/math-academy-id": "e-4705",
              ":question/problem": "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n",
              ":question/worked-solution": "First, we need to convert $A$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $A$ has $3$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $3.$"
            },
            ":knowledge-point/id": "1073953e-7e0a-5237-8533-8882b7772741",
            ":knowledge-point/title": "Finding the Number of Pivot Columns of a Matrix"
          },
          {
            ":db/id": 17592186124480,
            ":knowledge-point/canonical-example": {
              ":db/id": 17592186124293,
              ":question/id": "3ac076bd-5add-5c08-bb96-7b11c0a37d54",
              ":question/math-academy-id": "e-4706",
              ":question/problem": "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $B,$ given by\n\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\n",
              ":question/worked-solution": "First, we need to convert $B$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+\\left(-\\frac{2}{7}\\right){R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $B$ has $3$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th columns."
            },
            ":knowledge-point/id": "b1a557d6-52f3-5df3-8088-5b875296e72e",
            ":knowledge-point/title": "Finding the Pivot Columns of a Matrix"
          }
